### Non-blocking version
This version doesn't use `delay()`, so the loop can do other work while the LED blinks:

```cpp
const int LED_PIN = LED_BUILTIN;
const unsigned long INTERVAL_MS = 500;  // toggle every 500 ms, giving a 1 s period

unsigned long lastToggle = 0;
bool ledState = false;

void setup() {
  pinMode(LED_PIN, OUTPUT);
}

void loop() {
  unsigned long now = millis();
  if (now - lastToggle >= INTERVAL_MS) {  // safe across millis() rollover
    lastToggle = now;
    ledState = !ledState;
    digitalWrite(LED_PIN, ledState);
  }
  // other tasks can run here
}
